course: dictionary
lesson: 10346
title: Transition: change and link
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A transition is a change from one stage, place or state to another. «Next year Maya makes the transition from primary school to secondary school.» The word shows that something is moving from one stage to the next.
explain: In writing, a transition is a word or phrase that links ideas, like «however» or «next». «We played outside all afternoon. However, it started to rain.» The word however tells the reader that the idea is about to change.
explain: As a verb, to transition means to move or change from one stage to another: «The caterpillar will transition into a butterfly.» Look for the clues around the word to tell whether it is a noun or a verb.
fact: Transition means a change from one stage, place or state to another.
fact: «A smooth transition» means the change went well and was easy.
fact: When ice melts into water, it makes a transition from solid to liquid.
fact: Transition words such as «however», «next» and «first» join ideas together in writing.
fact: Moving up from primary school to secondary school is a big transition.
exercise: «Moving up to secondary school is a big transition.» What does transition mean here? | *A change from one stage to another | A long holiday | A type of school bus | A test you take at the end of the year
exercise: «However» is a transition word in writing. What is its job? | *To link ideas | To name a place | To end the story | To make a loud noise
exercise: When ice melts, it changes from solid to a new state. What state is the water in? | Solid | *Liquid | Frozen | Invisible
test: «The team made a smooth transition to the new classroom.» What does smooth transition mean? | The classroom was painted green | The team ran away from the classroom | The change was bumpy and loud | *The change went well and was easy
test: Which word is a transition word that links ideas? | jump | table | *next | happy
exam: Which sentence uses transition as a verb, meaning to change? | The transition was a long walk to school. | *The caterpillar will slowly transition into a butterfly. | Her favourite word is however. | The map shows a transition on the hill.
